===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*fuglaz}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|fugel}} ({{cog|fy|fûgel}}), {{cog|goh|fogal}} ({{cog|de|Vogel}}), {{cog|osx|fugal}} ({{cog|nds-de|Vagel|Vagel, Vogel}}), {{cog|odt|fogal}} ({{cog|nl|vogel}}), {{cog|non|fugl}} ({{cog|sv|fågel}}, {{cog|da|fugl}}), {{cog|got|𐍆𐌿𐌲𐌻𐍃}}. The Germanic base is a variant of {{m|gem-pro|*flugla-||fly}}, compare {{m|gem-pro|*fleuganą}} ({{cog|ang|flēogan}}).

